## Browser API rate limit (client-only)

**Set in `~/.ssh/be/.env`** — mirrored into the FE bundle at Vite dev/build via `fe/vite.config.mjs` (not `fe/.env`).

```bash
FE_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLE=true
FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_ACCESS_LIMIT=100
FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_TIMESLICE_SECONDS=60
FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_COOLDOWN_SECONDS=30
FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_COOLDOWN_ENABLED=true
FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_CONSOLE_LOG=false
```

| Variable | Value | Behavior |
|----------|-------|----------|
| `FE_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLE` | `true` | Master switch (`fe/src/config/clientApiRateLimitEnv.js`). `false` = no browser cooldown. |
| `FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_ACCESS_LIMIT` | `100` | Max API calls per timeslice per tab. |
| `FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_TIMESLICE_SECONDS` | `60` | Rolling window length. |
| `FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_COOLDOWN_SECONDS` | `30` | Cooldown after limit hit. |
| `FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_COOLDOWN_ENABLED` | `true` | Sub-switch; `false` = same as master off for gating. |
| `FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_CONSOLE_LOG` | `false` | DevTools logging when master enabled. |

After changes: restart **Vite** (`feall`). No PM2 restart unless you only changed backend-only keys.

